CONCLUSION
  drift lemma fires  <=>  r < 7.
  spread13_lonely closes  all r <= 13   (kps-S28, kernel-pure, one line).
  {r < 7} is a STRICT SUBSET of {r <= 13}  =>  the drift lemma is VACUOUS for the proof:
  it never fires on a case spread13_lonely leaves open.

THE OPEN REGIME r > 13:  local drift-absorbed embedding is IMPOSSIBLE
  r= 13: spread/Vmax = 0.9231 (teeth move 92.3% of a turn per ruler period);  need g > 1.857 > 1  IMPOSSIBLE
  r= 14: spread/Vmax = 0.9286 (teeth move 92.9% of a turn per ruler period);  need g > 2.000 > 1  IMPOSSIBLE
  r= 20: spread/Vmax = 0.9500 (teeth move 95.0% of a turn per ruler period);  need g > 2.857 > 1  IMPOSSIBLE
  r= 50: spread/Vmax = 0.9800 (teeth move 98.0% of a turn per ruler period);  need g > 7.143 > 1  IMPOSSIBLE

RESOLUTION OF THE 1/7-vs-2/7 TENSION
  The correct threshold is neither 1/7 nor 2/7: it is  g > (1/7) * (Vmax/Vmin),  ratio-dependent.
  g=1/7 needs r<1 (impossible);  g=2/7 needs r<2;  and g<=1 caps the whole local route at r<7.
  So the local slow-fast bridge dies at r>=7, strictly inside the regime spread13_lonely
  already handles.  hembed must be NON-LOCAL in the open regime r>13.

CONSISTENT with mac-mini-S64's exact counterexample (worst7Struct, Vmax=91, Vmin=9, r=10.1):
  good periods j=5,10,11 have NO lonely phi (exact max_phi minReach = 3/43, 2/31, 1/23 < 1/14),
  while a DISTANT j=25 is lonely (0.2306).  The lonely time is not at the good period.
